{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_033, acc 0.713) uses scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted fusion in a multimodal multiprofile setting. The image encoder dimension is completely unexplored in multimodal fusion—only resnet50 has been tested, and image-only resnet50 performed very poorly (0.208), suggesting the image signal may be underutilized. Config_039 swaps in imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings at their empirically best values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted). This directly tests whether a stronger, higher-capacity image encoder can improve the multimodal contribution. It is the most informative next step because: (1) it isolates the image encoder variable against the strongest known baseline, (2) it exploits the evidence that weighted fusion and transformer aggregation are beneficial, and (3) the answer—whether ViT-L helps or not—will clarify whether further investment in the image modality is worthwhile or whether the RNA modality is already capturing most of the signal. Under a limited budget, this single experiment resolves a major unexplored design axis while building on the most promising configuration."
}

